<article class="env-lemma" id="5E6DDE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5E6DDE">Lemma <span data-tag="5E6DDE">6.3.5.25</span>.</a> Let $\alpha : F \rightarrow G$ be a morphism in $\widehat{\Shv }(\LGeom ^{op})$, and assume that $G$ is representable by an $\infty $-topos $\calX $. Then $F$ is representable by an $\infty $-topos étale over $\calX $ if the following conditions are satisfied: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The morphism $\alpha $ is universal (in the sense of Definition <a href="/tag/63AF34" data-tag="63AF34">6.3.5.22</a>). 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
For every $\infty $-topos $\calY $, the homotopy fibers of the induced map $F(\calY ) \rightarrow G(\calY )$ are essentially small. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>